the-firm-as-one-program-57 : List Word
the-firm-as-one-program-57 = unlines (cons "- **Q4** The epistemic basis of prediction: no prior distribution, ever; exact inference over the present." (cons (quoted (cons "  Assuming a prior distribution is pure assumption rather than reality and cannot ground any claim of truth; a uniform prior is an even stronger ungrounded assumption than a reasoned one. Information " (cons "from tomorrow" (cons " is metaphysically nonsensical: tomorrow is undetermined now. [P1: Observation fibers: what a reading warrants, and when a participant is safe to act (hyperactivity v31 §1, §10.4)], [N2: The bridge to the rationality claim]" nil)))) (cons "  - **Q4.1** The object of analysis is not a prediction of price, since every action taken influences the world and the price." (cons "  - **Q4.2** The object is exact inference over the present: rationally exposing present information others have not." (cons "  - **Q4.3** We infer and predict the future into existence: when brains are called prediction machines, the prediction is the action; there is no separate action." (cons (quoted (cons "    predict: Latin praedicere, prae " (cons "before" (cons " + dicere " (cons "to say" (cons ", from the root *deyk- " (cons "to show, point out" (cons " (indicate, index, teach). infer: Latin inferre, " (cons "to carry into" (cons "." nil)))))))))) nil))))))
